# Zakaa-io Website — UI/UX Audit Action Items

## Accessibility

### A1: Fix light-mode text color contrast failures
- [x] A1.1: Replace `--text-muted: #000000` with `#52525b` in `globals.css` light theme
- [x] A1.2: Replace `--text-secondary: #000000` with `#3f3f46` in `globals.css` light theme
- [ ] A1.3: Verify all light-mode text colors meet WCAG AA 4.5:1 contrast ratio

### A2: Add light-mode override for `accent-text` utility
- [x] A2.1: Add `html[data-theme="light"] .accent-text { color: #4f46e5; }` to `globals.css`
- [x] A2.2: Verify `#4f46e5` on white background meets 4.5:1 contrast for normal text

### A3: Add `prefers-reduced-motion` support to FadeIn component
- [x] A3.1: Add `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` query in `globals.css`
- [x] A3.2: Disable opacity/transform transitions for users with reduced motion preference
- [x] A3.3: Update `FadeIn.tsx` to respect `prefers-reduced-motion` and skip animation when active

### A4: Replace `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in AIAgents chat messages
- [x] A4.1: Remove `dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: msg.text }}` from `AIAgents.tsx`
- [x] A4.2: Implement safe rendering using React `<strong>`, `<code>`, `<br/>` elements
- [x] A4.3: Add a simple HTML sanitizer or use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` only for trusted static content

### A4: Replace `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in AIAgents chat messages
- [x] A4.1: Remove `dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: msg.text }}` from `AIAgents.tsx`
- [x] A4.2: Implement safe rendering using React `<strong>`, `<code>`, `<br/>` elements
- [x] A4.3: Add a simple HTML sanitizer or use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` only for trusted static content

### A5: Add ARIA labels and form accessibility improvements
- [x] A5.1: Add `aria-label` to the chat widget language `<select>` element
- [x] A5.2: Add `aria-label` or `<label>` to all unlabeled form inputs across the site
- [x] A5.3: Add `aria-current="location"` to the active nav link in `Navbar.tsx`

### A6: Add keyboard navigation to navbar
- [x] A6.1: Implement arrow key navigation between nav links in `Navbar.tsx`
- [x] A6.2: Add `role="navigation"` and `aria-label` to the `<nav>` element
- [x] A6.3: Ensure all interactive elements are focusable and have visible focus indicators

### A7: Audit portal color consistency
- [x] A7.1: Replace Tailwind default `slate` colors in portal with site custom color tokens
- [x] A7.2: Ensure portal login page text contrast meets WCAG AA standards

## Usability

### U1: Fix `type="password"` on non-sensitive form inputs in Phase3Labs
- [x] U1.1: Change bearer token input from `type="password"` to `type="text"` with visibility toggle
- [x] U1.2: Change ticket title input from `type="password"` to `type="text"`
- [x] U1.3: Change affected service input from `type="password"` to `type="text"`
- [x] U1.4: Change ticket description textarea is already correct (no change needed)

### U2: Make AI chat widget collapsible/minimizable on mobile
- [x] U2.1: Add a minimize/dock button to `AIChatWidget.tsx`
- [x] U2.2: Ensure widget does not overlap content on mobile viewports
- [x] U2.3: Adjust `bottom` offset on mobile to avoid content occlusion

### U3: Add visual feedback for failed `#contact` scroll target
- [x] U3.1: Add null-check in `handleNav` functions across Navbar, Hero, Pricing, Footer
- [x] U3.2: Show a toast or inline message when scroll target is not found
- [x] U3.3: Extract `handleNav` into a shared `useSmoothScroll` hook to avoid duplication

### U4: Remove `no-underline` from navigational links
- [x] U4.1: Add underline or bottom-border to all `<a>` tags used as navigation
- [ ] U4.2: Reserve `no-underline` only for decorative or non-navigational text
- [ ] U4.3: Audit all components for remaining `no-underline` usage on clickable elements

### U5: Standardize interactive element patterns
- [ ] U5.1: Use `<button>` for all in-page scroll actions
- [ ] U5.2: Use `<a>` only for actual navigation (external links, page routes)
- [ ] U5.3: Add `role="button"` and keyboard handlers to any `<div>`/`<span>` used as interactive elements

## Visual Hierarchy

### V1: Simplify hero section content density
- [x] V1.1: Move stats row below the fold or reduce to 2 key metrics
- [ ] V1.2: Consider moving the Terminal component to a separate section
- [x] V1.3: Reduce hero heading size from `clamp(2.5rem,6vw,5rem)` to `clamp(2rem,5vw,4rem)`

### V2: Introduce secondary accent colors for visual differentiation
- [ ] V2.1: Add `accent-emerald` (`#10B981`) usage for success/positive signals
- [ ] V2.2: Add `accent-amber` (`#F59E0B`) usage for warnings/important signals
- [ ] V2.3: Reserve `accent-blue` (`#6366f1`) for primary actions only

### V3: Vary section layouts to break monotony
- [x] V3.1: Alternate section layouts (centered, left-aligned, split) across the homepage
- [ ] V3.2: Add a full-bleed or wide-background section for visual variety

### V4: Make "Most Popular" pricing badge more prominent
- [x] V4.1: Increase badge font size from `text-xs` to `text-sm`
- [x] V4.2: Change badge background from indigo to emerald for better contrast
- [x] V4.3: Increase Popular card scale from `md:scale-[1.03]` to `md:scale-[1.05]`

### V5: Add light-mode-specific styles for Terminal component
- [x] V5.1: Add `data-theme="light"` overrides for terminal background and text colors in `globals.css`
- [ ] V5.2: Ensure terminal code text is readable in both dark and light modes

## Consistency

### C1: Unify design tokens across marketing site and portal
- [ ] C1.1: Create a shared `theme.ts` or `tokens.css` file with all color, spacing, radius values
- [ ] C1.2: Update marketing site to consume from shared tokens
- [ ] C1.3: Update portal to consume from shared tokens instead of Tailwind default slate

### C2: Define and apply consistent border-radius scale
- [ ] C2.1: Define a radius scale (sm: 8px, md: 10px, lg: 12px, xl: 16px, 2xl: 20px)
- [ ] C2.2: Replace ad-hoc `rounded-[10px]`, `rounded-[14px]`, `rounded-[20px]` with scale tokens
- [ ] C2.3: Audit all components for radius consistency

### C3: Standardize font stack across marketing site and portal
- [ ] C3.1: Choose a single primary font (Inter or Geist) for both sites
- [ ] C3.2: Update portal `layout.tsx` to use Inter instead of Geist if Inter is chosen
- [ ] C3.3: Remove unused font imports from portal

### C4: Consolidate theme toggle logic into a single `useTheme` hook
- [ ] C4.1: Create `useTheme` hook in `lib/` that manages `data-theme`, localStorage, and `prefers-color-scheme`
- [ ] C4.2: Remove the inline `<script>` from `layout.tsx`
- [ ] C4.3: Update `ThemeToggle.tsx` to use the new `useTheme` hook
- [ ] C4.4: Ensure no flash of wrong theme on toggle

### C5: Extract duplicated `handleNav` into a shared utility
- [ ] C5.1: Create `useSmoothScroll` hook in `lib/` or `components/`
- [ ] C5.2: Update Navbar, Hero, Pricing, Footer to use the shared hook
- [ ] C5.3: Add null-check and fallback behavior (scroll to top or show toast) in the shared hook

### C6: Centralize `zakaa-navbar-control` custom utility
- [ ] C6.1: Document the `zakaa-navbar-control` class usage
- [ ] C6.2: Consider converting to a Tailwind `@apply` utility or design token class
